  ],
  "assertions": [
    "StreamStarted.initial_timestamp = 0 for a fresh instance; a late subscriber to an already-running instance would carry a nonzero mid-stream anchor (spec §4.4).",
    "PlaybackDiagnostics exercises every field type: fixed64 counters (little-endian on the wire), sint64 signed counters via zigzag varint (cumulative_lost = -2 encodes as varint 3; concealed_frames = +1440 as varint 2880), and uint32 scalars. Zero-valued fields (interval_lost, unknown_config drops) are proto3 defaults and are not encoded.",
    "Unsubscribe in PLAYING: the Server pushes StreamEnded(502, detail 'unsubscribed') FIRST, then UnsubscribeResponse(OK) — the spec §5.2 row fixes this order; state moves PLAYING -> READY.",
    "Unsubscribe is idempotent in general (duplicate/late Unsubscribe also gets OK, spec §5.2).",
    "A QUIC ACK or socket receive is not proof of decode: these Client-reported counters are the only playback evidence the Server gets (spec §9)."
  ]
}
